		<p>High Beam Assist is a function that automatically adjusts the headlamp range (switches between high beam and low beam) depending on the brightness of detected vehicles and certain road conditions.</p>
		<section>
			<title>Detecting sensor</title>
			<p>High Beam Assist (HBA) uses the front view camera. Please refer to <xref href="t00445.dita#t00445"/> for the sensor locations.</p>
			<note type="note">
				<ul>
					<li>
						<p>Always keep the front view camera in good condition to maintain optimal performance of High Beam Assist.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p>For more details on the precautions of the front view camera, refer to <xref href="t00446.dita#t00446"/>.</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
</concept>